#
# EXP-2: the trail does not flicker. The seam repaints at the return of
# the program's own back-buffer present, reached by every path that puts
# a screen up (`seam_explored.cpp`), and the risk only a run can answer
# is a repaint landing a moment late, which would show as the trail
# blinking off and on.
# A single leg, because a pair compares two runs and this is a claim
# about one run over time: with the party standing still and nothing
# pressed, fifty-one consecutive stills are the same screen.

about the fog holds still while the party does
kind single
program START.EXE
both code-wheel

# The code-wheel bypass is gated on the wheel itself (#115), pinned by
# digest because a document never enters this tree.
document 0db301aeac4d2ec1e63b409ca6d3c9d39c63381d6712ff2ce7edc0528c6586fd
seam explored
until 260000000
every 25

key A@7601
key Return@7651
key L@8951
key J@9201
key Up@10600
key Up@10750
key Up@10900
key Up@11050
key Up@11200
key Up@11350
key Up@11500
key Up@11650

# From the frame after the last step to the end of the run: the party is
# standing on the wilderness map inside the corridor it uncovered, with the
# fog round it, and nothing about the screen may change.
same 11750-13000
